  "keyNotes": "Contaminant (25 PPM CO) in No. 2 Entry: advance in No. 2 or the entries next to it (Rule 44B). Smoke in No. 2 inby Crosscut 3: lifeline. Smoldering fire at the battery charger in Crosscut 4: put it out before passing. Explosive mixture at the No. 1 Entry face is not near evidence of fire (no withdrawal). Timbers in No. 3 Entry are needed to reach the unconscious person under unsafe roof in Crosscut 5. Barricade in No. 4 inby Crosscut 5 answers: airlock and breach promptly.",
